# Secrets. .env carries the vision-model key, the database password and the
# operator login -- committing it is the whole compromise in one file.
# These are listed explicitly rather than relying on the generic .env rules
# below, because the point is too important to leave to a pattern.
.env
server/.env
vlm_eval/.apimart_key

# The template ships .env.* too. Keep the negation: .env.example is the
# deployment checklist and is meant to be committed.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Screenshots and crops of real people: the nine Quick Add captures, the
# 99-profile contact sheet and the 99 individual row crops cut from it. These
# are faces, display names and handles belonging to people who never agreed to
# be in a git history, and a git history is the one place you cannot delete
# them from later. Both directories are images only.
#
# The e2e suite supplies test/main/all99_3col.png per machine and skips when it
# is missing -- see server/test/sheet-fixture.ts.
#
# Both patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash. Written bare as `test/` the
# rule matches a directory named test at any depth, which silently swallowed
# server/test/ -- the suite's own source. sheet-fixture.ts was added to the
# working tree, skipped by `git add` without a word, and pushed in a state where
# three specs imported a file that was not in the commit.
/pages/
/test/

# Local runtime state, never an image or a repo
server/.storage/
server/api.log
server/api.err
# The worker's pair was missed when api.* was listed, so both were committed.
# `*.log` below does not help: it never matched .err, and neither pattern has
# any effect on a file that is already tracked.
server/worker.log
server/worker.err
vlm_eval/crops/
vlm_eval/results/

# Regenerated by roster_out.py / full_table.py from a stored run. They are
# output, not source -- and they list the same 99 real people by name and
# handle as the screenshots removed above, minus only the faces.
vlm_eval/full_roster.csv
vlm_eval/full_roster.md
vlm_eval/roster_with_nationality.csv
vlm_eval/roster_with_nationality.md
vlm_eval/side_by_side.csv

# Caddy's issued certificates
caddy-data/
caddy-config/

# Python (vlm_eval)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

